---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';
// DRAFT
---
<Tunnel title="Fresh Drive | Save My Gig!" status="Quick_Fix">
  <div class="review-flag">DRAFT, review pending.</div>
  <div class="step-label">Plan B</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Build tonight on a different drive</h2>

  <p>Build tonight on a known-good drive. Recover the sick one tomorrow.</p>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Get <strong>any other USB drive</strong>. Your spare, another DJ's, the venue's.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- THE MOST DANGEROUS INSTRUCTION ON THE SITE.
       The line above tells the DJ to BORROW a drive. The line below tells them
       to format it. Until now those two sat next to each other with nothing in
       between, on a screen reachable from five different places, none of which
       warned about this drive. That is a working route to erasing another DJ's
       library in the middle of their night. The warning is not optional and it
       goes BETWEEN the two instructions, not above them, because that is where
       the reader is when the decision is made. -->
  <div class="alert-card" style="margin:0 0 1.25rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</div>
    <div>
      <strong>If you borrowed this drive, stop and check with the owner.</strong>
      The next step erases it completely. Someone else's library is not
      expendable, and they may not know you are about to format it.
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Once you know the drive is empty or expendable, format it: <span class="mono">FAT32</span> + <span class="mono">MBR</span>.</li>
    <li>Export tonight's playlists from Rekordbox, or copy the music files you backed up.</li>
    <li>Verify: eject, replug, everything loads.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Is the fresh drive working?</p>

  <Choice step="qf_fresh_usb"
    a={{ href: '/saved?path=quick_fix&branch=fresh_usb', label: "YES, I AM READY", event: 'outcome_reached', data: { outcome: 'saved', path: 'quick_fix' } }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/critical', label: 'NO, OUT OF TIME', desc: 'Switch to the critical path: workarounds and survival mode.' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
